msgid "Project specific plugins"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In all the examples so far the plugins listed as `user scoped`. This means "
"that the plugins are global to the user. It is possible however to also have "
"`project scoped` plugins.\n"
"This is important as it allows:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Having project specific plugins"
msgstr ""

msgid "Overriding versions per project"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sharing the plugin catalog (via version control)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support extension provided plugins"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the `quarkus plug add` command is called from within a project, the "
"plugin is added to the project catalog, unless the `--user` options is used.\n"
"The plugin catalog is persisted in `.quarkus` in the root of the project. By "
"adding this folder to version control, the project plugin catalog is shared "
"between users of the project.\n"
"In this case, its a good idea to also include the actual plugin source files "
"in version control, or use a shared https://www.jbang.dev/[JBang] catalog."
msgstr ""

